    "updated_at": "2025-05-15T07:28:32Z",
    "body": "I see, I guess that does seem like a bug.\n\nAt this point I don't really understand what the intended architecture was here. CSP does indeed have some frame-ish destinations, but it also has initiators, and seems to imply that CSP should be using initiator instead of destination:\n\n> A [request](https://fetch.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-request)’s [initiator](https://fetch.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-request-initiator) is not particularly granular for the time being as other specifications do not require it to be. It is primarily a specification device to assist defining CSP and Mixed Content. It is not exposed to JavaScript. [[CSP]](https://fetch.spec.whatwg.org/#biblio-csp) [[MIX]](https://fetch.spec.whatwg.org/#biblio-mix)\n\nDo you know what existing browsers do?",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
