    "created_at": "2025-05-15T18:34:24Z",
    "updated_at": "2025-05-15T18:34:24Z",
    "body": "- Chromium [implementation](https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:content/browser/loader/navigation_url_loader_impl.cc;l=512;drc=ef122c1b7ca07ed5ea69ca69ba0837e63551c973;bpv=1;bpt=1) passing in `destination` into the function. It is propagated [from the caller](https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:content/browser/loader/navigation_url_loader_impl.cc;l=252;drc=ef122c1b7ca07ed5ea69ca69ba0837e63551c973;bpv=1;bpt=1) from `request_info`. It is set [when creating a navigation request](https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:content/browser/renderer_host/navigation_request.cc;l=1260;drc=ef122c1b7ca07ed5ea69ca69ba0837e63551c973;bpv=1;bpt=1) which calls [`GetDestinationFromFrameTreeNode`](https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:content/browser/renderer_host/navigation_request.cc?q=symbol%3A%5Cbcontent%3A%3AGetDestinationFromFrameTreeNode%5Cb%20case%3Ayes). It checks the element and changes the destination based on that, including iframes.\n- Webkit [implementation](https://github.com/WebKit/WebKit/blob/40ce4184c80e08e58d795efff16ed24d8ef42b30/Source/WebCore/Modules/fetch/FetchRequest.h#L67) where `destination` is stored in [`FetchOptions`](https://github.com/WebKit/WebKit/blob/40ce4184c80e08e58d795efff16ed24d8ef42b30/Source/WebCore/loader/FetchOptions.h#L59). It is set [when creating a request](https://github.com/WebKit/WebKit/blob/40ce4184c80e08e58d795efff16ed24d8ef42b30/Source/WebCore/loader/cache/CachedResourceLoader.cpp#L1118) which calls [`destinationForType`](https://github.com/WebKit/WebKit/blob/40ce4184c80e08e58d795efff16ed24d8ef42b30/Source/WebCore/loader/cache/CachedResourceLoader.cpp#L1035).\n- Gecko I am not sure where navigation happens (they don't comment it). I did find [`LoadInfo`]([nsDocShell.cpp](https://searchfox.org/mozilla-central/rev/b7b6aa5e8ffc27bc70d4c129c95adc5921766b93/docshell/base/nsDocShell.cpp#10474)) which is set [when loading a URI](https://searchfox.org/mozilla-central/rev/b7b6aa5e8ffc27bc70d4c129c95adc5921766b93/docshell/base/nsDocShell.cpp#10212) which calls [`DetermineContentType`](https://searchfox.org/mozilla-central/rev/b7b6aa5e8ffc27bc70d4c129c95adc5921766b93/docshell/base/nsDocShell.cpp#8246)\n\nIt seems that all browsers store this information in `{load,request}_info` and implement a switch function, either on the element type or from some other internal enum.",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
